<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila financial markets closed for Easter break.</title>
<headline>Manila financial markets closed for Easter break.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine financial markets are closed on Friday for the Easter holiday. Trading will resume on Monday.</p>
<p>Markets were also closed on Thursday. On Wednesday, the average call loan rate slipped to 9.9375 percent from 10.03125 percent after the Central Bank cut its overnight borrowing rate to 9.9 percent from 10.0 percent.</p>
<p>Likewise, the peso closed weaker at 26.367 against the dollar 26.355 due to the rate cut.</p>
<p>Philippine interbank offered rates were mostly higher except for the one-week rate which remained steady.</p>
<p>- Manila newsroom 63 2 8418938 Fax 8176267</p>
